  "body": "**What.** Measure the smallest singular value, and hence \u03ba, of the RT Jacobian on the resolving grids (32 \u00d7 101, 32 \u00d7 121) at D = 20\u201330, by inverse iteration with #105's solver at two precisions. Recommended by #105's subagent.\n\n**Why.** The f64 LU pivot ratio (5e12\u20131.4e17) saturates and is not \u03ba. #91 measured \u03ba only on coarse grids past D = 10, so the conditioning claim in RT_FORMULATION.md's verdict is not measured where the prototype now works.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).** The two precisions agree to 1e-6. A planted smallest singular value of 1e-20 is recovered. A 64-bit mutation must fail.\n\n**Depends on.** #105.\n",
